1
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:07,230
In modern warfare, firearms have become
increasingly specialized and diversified.

2
00:01:11,619 --> 00:01:19,320
As a result, weapons have been developed
for increasingly specialized purposes.

3
00:01:19,321 --> 00:01:24,380
These specialized firearms are used by
military special forces and counter-terrorism police.

4
00:01:38,874 --> 00:01:46,550
They are known as "Special Purpose Weapons."

5
00:01:46,551 --> 00:01:51,520
A submachine gun is designed to fire
pistol-caliber ammunition automatically.

6
00:01:51,594 --> 00:01:58,070
It is compact and offers excellent
controllability during automatic fire.

7
00:02:01,739 --> 00:02:09,440
Let's compare the M16 assault
rifle and the MP5 Sub-Machine Gun.

8
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:26,260
The submachine gun uses less powerful ammunition
and has a shorter effective range,

9
00:02:26,410 --> 00:02:29,670
making it well suited to close-range combat.

10
00:02:29,671 --> 00:02:32,586
This is particularly useful in urban areas,

11
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:35,312
where civilians may be present.

12
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:55,834
It is therefore used by special units
in many countries

13
00:02:55,858 --> 00:02:57,538
and for duties such as VIP protection.

14
00:03:15,690 --> 00:03:20,040
German Heckler & Koch MP5A3 submachine gun.

15
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:24,302
Based on the company's highly reliable G3 rifle,

16
00:03:24,326 --> 00:03:28,352
it is compact and lightweight.

17
00:03:57,190 --> 00:04:00,639
It inherits features from the G3, including

18
00:04:00,663 --> 00:04:04,502
Heckler & Koch's roller-delayed blowback system.

19
00:04:04,515 --> 00:04:08,780
It is highly regarded for its accuracy and handling.

20
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:13,850
In Germany it is used by counter-terrorism
units such as GSG 9 and SEK.

21
00:04:28,830 --> 00:04:30,409
It is also used by special units
in many other countries, including

22
00:04:30,433 --> 00:04:32,142
SWAT teams in the United States
and the SAS in the United Kingdom.

23
00:04:32,143 --> 00:04:38,630
Israel's Uzi is one of the world's
best-known submachine guns.

24
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:49,920
The magazine is housed inside the pistol grip,
contributing to its compact layout.

25
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:53,413
It uses a simple blowback action
with a telescoping bolt,

26
00:04:53,437 --> 00:04:56,582
helping keep the weapon compact
and controllable.

27
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:19,740
Its stamped-steel construction
is well suited to mass production.

28
00:05:20,130 --> 00:05:24,018
Since its introduction in 1951, it has become

29
00:05:24,042 --> 00:05:27,942
one of the classic modern submachine-gun designs

30
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:30,560
and influenced many later weapons.

31
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:44,811
It has been used in Israel, Germany,
the Netherlands, Belgium and other countries.

32
00:05:44,835 --> 00:05:47,912
Netherlands, Belgium,
and other countries.

33
00:05:48,375 --> 00:05:52,730
In the United States it has also been used
by the Secret Service for presidential protection.

34
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:11,970
Brazil's Taurus MT-12AD submachine gun.

35
00:06:14,810 --> 00:06:22,810
Taurus produced the Beretta M12S under license
and further developed the design,

36
00:06:23,110 --> 00:06:27,520
improving its safety features and adding
an ejection-port cover.

37
00:06:59,945 --> 00:07:03,666
It uses a distinctive tubular receiver
and stamped components,

38
00:07:03,690 --> 00:07:07,882
with a separate foregrip beneath the barrel.

39
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:21,234
The Taurus MT-12AD and original Beretta M12S
have been used

40
00:07:21,258 --> 00:07:25,192
in Italy and in countries throughout
South America and Africa.

41
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:44,880
Let's compare the accuracy of an assault rifle
with that of a sniper rifle.

42
00:07:52,210 --> 00:07:55,760
A standard G3 assault rifle with iron sights
and a PSG1 sniper rifle

43
00:07:55,784 --> 00:07:59,822
fire at targets 100 meters away.

44
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:08,808
A sniper rifle is intended for precision fire
against terrorists

45
00:08:08,832 --> 00:08:12,732
or important battlefield targets at long range.

46
00:08:19,570 --> 00:08:27,570
In this way, there is a
big difference in accuracy.

47
00:08:39,765 --> 00:08:47,740
American sniper rifle: Remington Model 700.

48
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:58,945
It is a manually operated bolt-action rifle
designed to minimize movement

49
00:08:58,969 --> 00:09:02,792
and maximize accuracy.

50
00:09:03,129 --> 00:09:07,710
Since its introduction in 1962,
it has been highly regarded.

51
00:09:30,769 --> 00:09:38,570
The Model 700 series has been offered
in numerous configurations.

52
00:09:39,019 --> 00:09:44,220
The U.S. Marine Corps adopted a
7.62 mm NATO version as the basis for its sniper rifle.

53
00:10:04,389 --> 00:10:11,040
Heckler & Koch PSG1 sniper rifle.

54
00:10:41,449 --> 00:10:43,875
Based on the G3 system, the PSG1 is one of
Heckler & Koch's premier precision rifles,

55
00:10:43,899 --> 00:10:47,619
and its semi-automatic action allows
an immediate follow-up shot.

56
00:11:10,879 --> 00:11:14,017
It includes features such as a forward assist
for quietly closing the action,

57
00:11:14,041 --> 00:11:18,121
and a rigid scope mounting system designed
to maintain accuracy.

58
00:11:26,659 --> 00:11:30,230
Although semi-automatic, it is regarded as a
sniper rifle with accuracy comparable to bolt-action designs.

59
00:11:30,254 --> 00:11:33,522
with a accuracy that is
not inferior to bolt action.

60
00:11:47,779 --> 00:11:48,241
It has been adopted by GSG 9, SEK

61
00:11:48,265 --> 00:11:50,185
and other counter-terrorism units.

62
00:12:02,990 --> 00:12:10,990
A representative Eastern Bloc sniper rifle,
the Dragunov SVD,

63
00:12:23,569 --> 00:12:26,749
uses a gas-operated action

64
00:12:26,773 --> 00:12:30,232
with a rotating bolt.

65
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:40,040
It was developed in the Soviet Union
and adopted in 1963.

66
00:12:48,959 --> 00:12:56,260
Licensed versions have also been produced
in China and Eastern Europe.

67
00:13:14,269 --> 00:13:19,182
Micro-submachine guns, reduced to roughly
the size of a large pistol,

68
00:13:19,594 --> 00:13:23,520
provide tremendous close-range firepower

69
00:13:23,919 --> 00:13:30,200
and are used in the final stages of
counter-terrorism operations.

70
00:13:47,789 --> 00:13:50,327
The Ingram M11 is only 24.8 cm long

71
00:13:50,351 --> 00:13:52,902
and has a cyclic rate of roughly
20 rounds per second.

72
00:14:15,634 --> 00:14:17,880
It has been used by special units in countries
including the United States,

73
00:14:17,904 --> 00:14:20,422
United Kingdom, Bolivia, Colombia and Israel.

74
00:14:26,309 --> 00:14:33,610
Finland's Jatimatic micro-submachine gun.

75
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:40,437
To improve controllability during firing,

76
00:14:40,461 --> 00:14:44,552
the bolt travels upward at an angle.

77
00:15:00,579 --> 00:15:03,338
Its cocking handle, safety and foregrip
combine multiple functions,

78
00:15:03,362 --> 00:15:06,292
helping reduce the total number of parts.

79
00:15:23,609 --> 00:15:26,952
For a micro-submachine gun, it makes unusual use

80
00:15:26,976 --> 00:15:29,772
of both stamped steel and polymer components.

81
00:15:30,209 --> 00:15:34,650
It incorporates several distinctive design ideas.

82
00:15:54,659 --> 00:15:59,260
The Micro Uzi is a smaller and lighter
version of the Uzi submachine gun.

83
00:16:07,519 --> 00:16:11,269
It is the smallest model in the Uzi family,

84
00:16:11,293 --> 00:16:15,432
measuring about 23 cm with the stock folded.

85
00:16:16,119 --> 00:16:23,010
It weighs only 1.9 kg and has a cyclic rate
of roughly 22 rounds per second.

86
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:51,980
In Israel, the Micro Uzi has been used
for bodyguard and security duties.

87
00:16:57,640 --> 00:17:05,640
The Para Pistol Mk 7A4 is a compact version
of the Sterling submachine gun.

88
00:17:10,510 --> 00:17:14,334
Its barrel is shortened and the stock removed,

89
00:17:14,358 --> 00:17:18,522
giving an overall length of 38 cm
and a weight of 2.2 kg.

90
00:17:36,519 --> 00:17:40,246
The Para Pistol series is based on the Sterling,
with variants including

91
00:17:40,270 --> 00:17:44,482
the long-barreled Mk 7A8 and
the commercial semi-automatic Mk 7C4.

92
00:17:52,929 --> 00:17:57,080
It has been used by special units
including the British SAS.

93
00:17:59,934 --> 00:18:06,260
Czechoslovakia's vz. 61 Škorpion.

94
00:18:09,459 --> 00:18:13,312
Its distinctive wire shoulder stock folds
forward over the top of the weapon,

95
00:18:13,336 --> 00:18:17,372
reducing its overall length to about 27 cm.

96
00:18:22,259 --> 00:18:26,810
It is a compact submachine gun
chambered for 7.65 mm ammunition.

97
00:18:27,459 --> 00:18:31,112
It is designed for good controllability
during automatic fire.

98
00:18:31,136 --> 00:18:34,202
Its rate-reduction mechanism helps keep
the firing rate manageable.

99
00:18:42,799 --> 00:18:46,062
It has been used by Czechoslovak
special forces and police,

100
00:18:46,086 --> 00:18:49,712
and was also produced under license
in Yugoslavia.

101
00:18:56,969 --> 00:19:04,870
Shotguns, which can fire multiple projectiles
with a single shot, have long been used for hunting.

102
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:12,014
Shorter, specialized shotguns are also used
by police and military forces,

103
00:19:12,038 --> 00:19:16,242
where they are often called riot guns
or combat shotguns.

104
00:19:19,279 --> 00:19:23,193
Let's compare the characteristics of a submachine gun,
frequently used in counter-terrorism,

105
00:19:23,217 --> 00:19:27,142
with those of shotgun ammunition.

106
00:19:58,054 --> 00:20:01,606
The submachine gun offers greater penetration,

107
00:20:01,630 --> 00:20:05,342
while the shotgun delivers greater
close-range stopping effect.

108
00:20:32,979 --> 00:20:36,728
The Maverick Model 88 is a conventional
pump-action shotgun

109
00:20:36,752 --> 00:20:40,642
with a six-round capacity.

110
00:20:56,570 --> 00:21:00,500
The Model 88 was sold under the Maverick brand

111
00:21:00,524 --> 00:21:04,582
using a design derived from Mossberg's Model 500.

112
00:21:27,719 --> 00:21:30,748
It is used by American police agencies

113
00:21:30,772 --> 00:21:33,932
and is also sold commercially
for security and sporting use.

114
00:21:58,309 --> 00:21:59,633
The Italian Franchi SPAS-15 combat shotgun

115
00:21:59,657 --> 00:22:01,617
was developed from the outset
with military use in mind.

116
00:22:05,099 --> 00:22:09,112
Introduced in 1987, it can operate in either
pump-action or semi-automatic mode

117
00:22:09,136 --> 00:22:12,562
and uses a detachable box magazine.

118
00:22:36,420 --> 00:22:40,655
With these modern features it serves as
a powerful police and military shotgun,

119
00:22:40,679 --> 00:22:44,432
and has been used primarily by
Italian and other European forces.

120
00:23:19,390 --> 00:23:23,603
The South African-designed Protecta shotgun
uses a distinctive 12-round

121
00:23:23,627 --> 00:23:27,402
revolving cylinder, providing substantial capacity.

122
00:23:38,539 --> 00:23:42,390
The South African design was produced
in several configurations.

123
00:23:42,414 --> 00:23:46,202
Its large revolving magazine is its
most distinctive feature.

124
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:55,218
In the United States, a related version

125
00:23:55,242 --> 00:23:59,242
was marketed under the name Streetsweeper.

126
00:24:14,519 --> 00:24:21,870
For covert attacks or counter-terrorist operations,
a submachine gun may be fitted with a suppressor.

127
00:24:39,619 --> 00:24:43,599
A suppressed submachine gun reduces the sound
and visible signature of firing,

128
00:24:43,623 --> 00:24:47,282
making it more difficult to determine
the shooter's location.

129
00:24:47,519 --> 00:24:55,220
It can therefore be useful during the opening
stages of certain special operations.

130
00:24:58,699 --> 00:25:06,550
The MP5SD2 is an MP5 variant
with an integral suppressor.

131
00:25:06,940 --> 00:25:10,806
Its integral suppressor works together with
barrel ports and internal baffles

132
00:25:10,830 --> 00:25:14,952
to provide substantial sound reduction.

133
00:25:36,409 --> 00:25:40,399
It has been used by units such as the British SAS,
U.S. Delta Force,

134
00:25:40,423 --> 00:25:44,272
and military and police special units
in many countries.

135
00:25:52,770 --> 00:26:00,770
Sterling Mk 5 suppressed submachine gun.

136
00:26:01,669 --> 00:26:05,580
In British military service it is designated L34A1.

137
00:26:08,259 --> 00:26:16,160
Based on the Sterling L2A3,
it was developed during the 1960s.

138
00:26:17,299 --> 00:26:20,951
It has been used by British special units
such as the SAS and SBS

139
00:26:20,975 --> 00:26:24,712
and has also been exported to other countries.

140
00:26:44,289 --> 00:26:49,890
Its suppressor is integral to the weapon.

141
00:26:50,289 --> 00:26:54,020
It uses expansion chambers and baffles
to reduce the report.

142
00:27:36,884 --> 00:27:40,924
Among special-purpose weapons are a few designs

143
00:27:40,948 --> 00:27:44,872
with highly unusual forms created
for very specialized roles.

144
00:27:49,049 --> 00:27:57,050
This is an MP5K concealed in an attaché case,
developed for discreet VIP protection.

145
00:27:58,709 --> 00:28:06,110
A rifle-mounted 40 mm grenade launcher.

146
00:28:18,129 --> 00:28:21,553
It can fire various types of 40 mm ammunition,

147
00:28:21,577 --> 00:28:25,642
including specialized and less-lethal rounds.

148
00:28:40,619 --> 00:28:44,370
Submachine guns normally use pistol ammunition,
but compact weapons using

149
00:28:44,394 --> 00:28:48,282
more powerful specialized cartridges
have also been developed.

150
00:28:54,769 --> 00:29:02,132
Belgian FN's P90 personal defense weapon,
completed in 1988.

151
00:29:02,319 --> 00:29:07,420
Its unusual magazine system and bullpup layout
allow a very compact overall design.

152
00:29:07,969 --> 00:29:11,530
The ejection port is located on the underside
of the receiver,

153
00:29:11,554 --> 00:29:15,062
making the weapon equally convenient
for right- or left-handed shooters.

154
00:29:16,800 --> 00:29:20,743
It uses the newly developed
5.7×28 mm cartridge,

155
00:29:20,767 --> 00:29:24,812
stored horizontally across the top of the weapon.

156
00:29:25,249 --> 00:29:28,664
It offers high penetration and useful range

157
00:29:28,688 --> 00:29:32,562
while keeping recoil relatively low.

158
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:44,890
As a personal defense weapon positioned between
a pistol and a rifle,

159
00:29:44,914 --> 00:29:48,692
its new concept attracted considerable attention.

160
00:29:49,229 --> 00:29:56,480
The MC51, a compact carbine based on the G3.

161
00:30:01,950 --> 00:30:05,980
The British firm FR Ordnance International

162
00:30:06,004 --> 00:30:09,962
shortened the G3 system while retaining
the powerful 7.62 mm NATO cartridge.

163
00:30:19,939 --> 00:30:23,631
The AKS-74U is a shortened version of
the Soviet AKS-74

164
00:30:23,655 --> 00:30:27,852
and uses the 5.45×39 mm cartridge.

165
00:30:43,870 --> 00:30:47,704
It has been used by Soviet and Russian
special units including Spetsnaz

166
00:30:47,728 --> 00:30:51,882
and has also seen widespread use
throughout Eastern Europe.

167
00:31:12,350 --> 00:31:16,214
As modern society becomes more complex,

168
00:31:16,238 --> 00:31:20,362
urban crime and terrorism take
increasingly varied forms.

169
00:31:22,850 --> 00:31:26,877
To respond to these threats,

170
00:31:26,901 --> 00:31:30,862
new special-purpose weapons may continue
to be developed in the future.

171
00:37:29,410 --> 00:37:37,410
Guns of the World Vol. 1: Handguns.

172
00:37:41,340 --> 00:37:48,990
The first volume, Handguns, features
the Beretta 92F and Glock 17,

173
00:37:49,440 --> 00:37:54,010
among the world's most notable
modern semi-automatic pistols.

174
00:37:54,710 --> 00:37:59,150
It also covers the Smith & Wesson Model 629,
Colt Anaconda and other

175
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:07,400
modern .44 Magnum revolvers.

176
00:38:22,950 --> 00:38:33,630
Historical pistols such as the Luger P08,
unusual specialty guns and fully automatic pistols

177
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:37,210
are included among 27 firearms
demonstrated on the range.

178
00:38:44,480 --> 00:38:52,480
Guns of the World Vol. 1: Handguns
explores the appeal of the handgun.

179
00:38:52,630 --> 00:38:57,310
Guns of the World Vol. 1: Handguns.

180
00:39:37,755 --> 00:39:45,530
Guns of the World Vol. 2:

181
00:39:45,630 --> 00:39:53,470
Military Armaments, covering weapons
from 5.56 mm to 12.7 mm,

182
00:39:53,471 --> 00:39:55,770
including rifles and machine guns.

183
00:39:56,070 --> 00:39:59,580
An introduction to modern military small arms.

184
00:40:17,630 --> 00:40:21,618
The futuristic German G11
caseless-ammunition rifle

185
00:40:21,642 --> 00:40:25,642
is shown in detail on video.

186
00:40:30,430 --> 00:40:34,605
Also featured is the Minimi SAW,
adopted by the U.S. military

187
00:40:34,629 --> 00:40:38,442
and selected as a squad-support weapon
by the Japan Self-Defense Forces.

188
00:41:02,690 --> 00:41:10,440
Guns of the World Vol. 2:
Military Armaments.

189
00:41:10,515 --> 00:41:15,390
A detailed look at modern assault rifles
and other military small arms.
